-        "note": "PLACEHOLDER. THE SHAPE CARRIES EVIDENCE AND EVERY NUMBER IN IT IS INVENTED, and the two must not be confused \u2014 the same distinction miller_house's footprint note draws. What is attested is the composition, from the only description of this building anybody wrote: 'a substantial, compact little building of logs hewed and squared, with a centre, two wings, and, strictly speaking, two tails, since, when there was found no more room for additions at the sides, they were placed in the rear, whereon a vacant spot could be found. These appendages did not mar the symmetry of the whole, as viewed from the front.' This polygon is that sentence drawn: a centre block projecting one metre forward of two flanking wings, so the front reads symmetrical, and two tails running back from the rear of the centre. The dimensions \u2014 a 5 m centre, 4 m wings, 1.5 m tails, a 13 x 9 m envelope \u2014 are chosen to suit the words 'compact little building' and are supported by nothing. Mrs. Callis's 'two large rooms' describes the house in 1816, before the wings and tails, and is the only interior evidence of any kind. NOTE WHAT THE MESH DOES WITH THIS: the log_dwelling archetype masses the polygon's BOUNDING BOX, so the visitor sees a plain 13 x 9 m rectangle and the composition this polygon draws is not built \u2014 the re-entrant corners beside the tails and beside the wings are filled in. That is admitted in docs/LIBERTIES.md rather than hidden, and it is the same limitation L27 records for Miller's house. To resolve: any plan, any dimension, or the Chicago Democrat's advertisements for the agency's buildings. T-2374 SUPERSESSION: the opt-in the connected room layout now builds five rooms whose union is this polygon, rather than its bounding box. The preceding paragraph describes the prior mesh limitation; its dimension and date cautions still apply."
+        "note": "T-2374 final bounded reconstruction: the text-attested centre, two symmetrical wings and two rear tails occupy a 9 by 4.5 m envelope. The 5 m centre is retained; each former 4 m wing is narrowed to 2 m and its front recessed 1 m behind the central front. The central room is 3.5 m deep, and each 1.5 m wide rear tail runs 1 m back. These are choices within Wau-Bun's compact five-part composition and the small keyed panorama's dominant front gable and subordinate visible side gable, not measured historic dimensions or a survey. Room-coordinate rebasing keeps the polygon at local zero; position and rotation are unchanged. The central openings retain their earlier relative offsets, count, heights and depths. The generator builds the exact union, including re-entrant corners. The unseen wing, tails and continuation to July 1835 remain reconstructed. Supersedes the former 13 by 9 m trial; see L-cobweb-completion-2374."
