+# Cobweb Castle — final two-picture review
+
+Both canonical views are **matches under T-3153**, with no open differences,
+after direct inspection of the complete actual source/native pairs and fixed
+8× inspection crops. This is the stopping-rule verdict, not pixel identity or
+a recovered historical camera.
+
+The genuine MASTER is `df10931a6be875df6b9ca2fa6a4a9c1edbe5e4d2b672771edfc1c9971e506b5b`
+(195392 bytes), built in native run42745792113 from source
+`64a752353bc66fa6bfa58c853b90c32625f7b739` and adopted through
+`9dd9ba7ddd22c6ff87e52522497205f62133fa1f`. Exact camera, picture, pair,
+raw-render and match hashes are in `ACCEPTANCE-RECEIPT.json`. The original
+as-generated unreviewed records, raw PNGs and logs remain externally retained
+under `/tmp/nov10-cobweb-complete/after/`; no generated result was silently
+restamped as though it already carried a review.
+
+The actual new native reads as a dominant front gable, receding main roof,
+smaller lower side gable and one roof stack, replacing the broad transverse
+trial and exterior stack pair. The three existing front marks and partial
+board band remain; the dark recesses are clear. The five-room composition,
+9×4.5 m envelope, exact roof junctions, sections and unseen rear adjuncts stay
+reconstructed. Source/text limits remain on the card and in the liberty.
+
+The keyed cut and companion lithograph disagree visibly about lower-mark
+lengths, side-gable foreshortening and the small wing mark's height. The keyed
+view governs the grounded marks and lower side-roof hierarchy. Those remaining
+picture/pose disagreements are **within tolerance** under T-3153; they are
+explicitly recorded rather than called new measurements. Approximate front
+fits have1.009/1.724px coordinate RMS at roughly2px reading uncertainty.
+Monochrome paper and hatching cannot attest paint, exact colour, glazing,
+finish dates, hidden rear forms or unchangedJuly1835appearance.
+
+The keyed panorama's existing source is
+`kinzie_1857_chicago_1831_panorama` (verified1881reproduction crediting1857 and
+depicting1831). The held unkeyed companion uses
+`kinzie_waubun_1831_unkeyed_panorama`, retaining the repository inventory's
+qualified Sarony/Wau-Bun1856attribution and existing public-domain finding.
+They are related reproductions, not independent witnesses. Both diagnostic
+cameras withhold invented historical From-this-spot navigation.
+
+Actual oldMASTER3abae40e and both BEFORE pairs are retained under
+`/tmp/nov10-cobweb-complete/before/`. The companion camera's later source-id and
+solve-text correction changed no render parameter or source pixel. Its true
+old BEFORE camera hash and metadata-only transition remain separately recorded
+in `POST-NATIVE-CAMERA-METADATA-RECEIPT.json`; it was not relabelled as a capture
+with new bytes. The keyed camera bytes stayed exact throughout.
+
+The reviewer uses a common flat plane and one building. Published terrain,
+rederived woodpile clearance, real Sources/Images/Liberties cards, desktop/phone
+runtime, integrated full gate and original-ticket/dev-merge completion remain
+separate parent-owned qualifications.
