+# T-2380: complete the source-informed jail core
+
+The independently public-domain Gale/Trowbridge 1902 illustration, explicitly captioned 1836, is the clearest whole-compound depiction. The actual full uncropped image and both current full comparisons were read; a rotation and magnified detail were used only as reading aids, with source bytes unchanged. Its log gable includes one upright barred-looking light with a horizontal crossing member, and its wall/roof stand substantially above the palisade. The prior 2.66 m eave/12 degree roof is a low proxy that does not reproduce that visible form.
+
+Adopt a 3.35 m eave and 28 degree gable on the unchanged 6.096 x 4.572 m reconstructed footprint (ridge 4.5655 m). Continue the existing hewn-course/chink material through the gables; add one 0.48 x 0.85 m dark light on the east gable beside the keeper, three upright members and one horizontal crossing member. Numeric dimensions, upright count/material, compass and July continuity remain reconstructed. No new cell, storey, interior floor, surveyed setback or household is asserted. The keeper and enclosure are untouched. The `picture_layout` keyword defaults to None for all other outbuildings, and invalid names/shapes/low roofs are refused.
+
+## Why this is allowed in the July scene
+
+Gale p51 places the jail, palisade and Beach's partly enclosed house in an 1835-framed recollection, but the illustration says 1836. The model makes a bounded continuity choice for appearance; it does not alter the source date, assert an exact July condition or date an undated addition. Andreas 1884 shows a conflicting hip/pyramidal cap and different domestic elevation. Both cannot be imposed simultaneously on one building; select the clearer detailed witness for the visible gable and retain Andreas as source disagreement within tolerance under AGENTS R11/T-3153. The drawing's apparent core flues are also absent in Andreas, and no July original-cell hearth or stack count is established. No later separate oaken cell or fall 1835 courthouse is backdated merely to fill a composition. The independently verified 1902 artwork, not a rights-held later copy, supplies this work.
+
+## Current evidence and required final review
+
+The pre-choice cameras/matches and actual 2.44 m fence side-by-sides are preserved in `history/20261110-before-core-gale-choice/`. The new Gale diagnostic eye is northeast, so it can show the pictured east gable and keeper end; camera/principal point are framing choices, never historical optics. The source page remains entire and unchanged. Andreas remains a full context image whose later courthouse is excluded by the July date.
+
+Actual producer CPU controls compare vertices, faces, confidence and material specifications against the preceding producer for all 243 other buildable outbuilding phases: exact. One existing historic brick courthouse phase is already refused by the outbuilding vocabulary and is reported separately. Forge and cargo owners pass. Four invalid layout variants are refused. These are producer controls, not Blender exports, browser screenshots or photo acceptance. The opt-in core adds 204 vertices including clipped gable chink strips, framing, three uprights and one crossbar.
+
+The parent run will execute the single combined pinned native batch, compile official sidecars/registries, refresh both actual native full comparisons, inspect desktop/phone street views, and record the final T-3153 verdict. Neither match record is promoted unseen. Source camera/scale disagreement alone is within tolerance; physical missing/wrong-shaped elements over the visitor bar must be fixed. The native family must pass default output controls before any source-input freshness rebind is accepted.
+
+An actual keeper-master triangle-ray control found that the first near northeast eye (24,18,1.7) hid78 of91 light samples behind the keeper roof. The final diagnostic eye (18,28,1.7), bearing210degrees, leaves all91 samples unobstructed by that actual keeper master. This bounded camera correction changes no model or site dimensions. It is CPU visibility evidence, not a native image-match result.
+
+## Actual final native image review
+
+The adopted98740B core (SHA2b8cb0d6…) and unchanged keeper were rendered through both exact retained diagnostic cameras with the native2.44m enclosure; both real commands exited0. Full pairs/raws and before/after input receipts are retained. Direct review confirms the exposed taller gable/hewn wall and upright inset. In the original1112×1645 Gale raw the inset lies approximatelyx425–477,y1010–1028, above keeper and fence. Fine three-upright/crossbar separation is not individually sharp at this oblique pose and is accepted only as below0.3m/projective detail underT3153. Both canonical views now match with no open visitor-visible discrepancy; Andreas/Gale source conflict, full context framing and1836-versus-July continuity remain explicit limits. This image review does not claim published terrain/walking or full runtime acceptance.
