+  "verdict": "differs",
+  "differences": [
+    {
+      "what": "Previously absent high plank palisade is now present in the actual native enclosure render. Gale p.51 supplies the kind/existence; overall3.05m height, compact outline and stock are declared reconstructions, not picture measurements. HEIGHT TRIAL 2026-11-10 (T-2380): the reconstructed overall height is now 2.44 m; 3.05 m describes the preceding comparison. Neither number is a measured historic fence height.",
+      "status": "fixed"
+    },
+    {
+      "what": "The actual native palisade now has pointed closed-board heads matching the pictured top form. Exact point rise and stock dimensions remain reconstructed.",
+      "status": "fixed"
+    },
+    {
+      "what": "The keeper house pictured partly within the compound is absent. Its footprint, original-cell relationship and July1835 continuity are unresolved; no anonymous house is relabelled or invented in this increment. RESOLVED 2026-11-03 (T-2380): The keeper house is now built and rendered in the group: log_jail_keeper_house__frame_1835.glb. Andreas draws the small white house beside the jail from a different side than Gale; the built elevation follows Gale, and that disagreement is recorded below rather than reconciled.",
+      "status": "fixed"
+    },
+    {
+      "what": "The pictured compound enclosure/gate relationship extends around the keeper house. The current compact enclosure and open doorway-aligned passage do not reproduce that whole compound or its hung gate. Layout and gate attribution remain unresolved. RESOLVED 2026-11-03 (T-2380): The continuous palisade front and the low house-side gate are now rendered. Their layout is reconstruction.",
+      "status": "fixed"
+    },
+    {
+      "what": "Andreas shows a hip/pyramidal rear cap, conflicting with Gale\u2019s taller gable. The mostly concealed original jail core/later-cell identity is unresolved; the post-July courthouse is deliberately absent from the July scene.",
+      "status": "within tolerance"
+    },
+    {
+      "what": "Provisional compound framing, distance and principal point are diagnostic choices. The full source is uncropped; common flat ground is a review adapter. This is not a solved source camera or a historical From this spot location, and neither pixel scale nor perspective disagreement is promoted into a metric geometry error.",
+      "status": "within tolerance"
+    },
+    {
+      "what": "The prior 3.05 m palisade concealed almost all of the retained jail core. FIXED IN PART 2026-11-10 (T-2380): at this unchanged authored camera the reconstructed 2.44 m palisade now leaves a shallow band of the existing core roof visible above the fence. This fixes complete concealment only; the source's taller exposed core/cap profile remains different. Core/keeper models, placement, grade plane, camera and full source are unchanged. Neither fence height nor the retained core form is measured from this diagnostic composition.",
+      "status": "fixed"
+    },
+    {
+      "what": "The newly exposed retained low roof does not reproduce the plate's tall log core and cap above the fence. The 2.44 m fence trial does not resolve that form/identity disagreement with Gale or date the pictured compound to July 1835. The post-July courthouse remains deliberately absent.",
+      "status": "open"
+    },
+    {
+      "what": "Scale and placement in frame differ grossly: the plate's jail group stands close behind the courthouse at the right of a near view, while the render puts the compound small and far off at the right edge. The camera here is diagnostic_only and was never solved to this plate, so this is a framing difference and is not promoted to a geometry error.",
+      "status": "open"
+    },
+    {
+      "what": "The plate's dominant subject, the brick Cook County court-house, is deliberately absent from the render: it was erected in the fall of 1835 and the county moved in toward the end of October, after the 1835-07-01 scene date. This is a date decision, not a modelling gap.",
+      "status": "within tolerance"
+    },
+    {
+      "what": "The actual native palisade already has separate 254 mm boards, 6 mm gaps and 127 mm pointed heads; no stock or material changes are made here. The distant diagnostic render still reads as a broad dark fence rather than the plate's visibly separated vertical members. Finish and stock legibility remain unresolved. The monochrome plate supplies no literal paint colour.",
+      "status": "open"
+    },
+    {
+      "what": "The keeper house's end gable took the roof-shingle material rather than wall boarding (see the Gale view, which is the plate that shows this end). FIXED 2026-11-04 (T-2380) by the same material-role change. In THIS plate the jail group is small at the right edge and the keeper's gable spans a few dozen pixels (93 px changed), so this view neither shows nor tests the correction; it is recorded here only so the two records do not disagree about the model.",
+      "status": "fixed"
+    }
+  ],
+  "_how": "verdict is unreviewed | differs | matches, set by whoever compared the side-by-side with the picture; each difference is {what, status: open | fixed | not shown | within tolerance | owner ruling} \u2014 open only if a street visitor would notice it (over about 1 ft, missing, mis-shaped, miscounted, wrong material or colour), else within tolerance (T-3153); owner ruling where the owner asked the build to depart from the picture (T-3236). A ticket whose ## Image gate names this building does not close while it is not \"matches\" (tools/image_gate.mjs)."
+}
